I was playing around trying to get the high score here, when I ran into a 
whole lot of strange behavior.  Because some of it is related to my efforts 
towards the upper reaches of the high score board, it will no doubt contain
some spoilers.  Of course, I find it hard to believe that anyone reading this
news group would object to being exposed to a spoiler.  Then again, I'll be 
polite and include a spoiler alert.  I would really appreciate some answers
to my questions.

****SPOILERS****

To get the dilithium I need for the high score, which I figure to be around
250,000 crystals, I have been turning monsters into statues and breaking the 
statues up with spells of force bolt.  I then polymorph the rocks until they
become dilithium.  In a past attempt, I was doing this by wielding cockatrice
corpses, and keeping them fresh by putting them in an ice chest when they 
weren't needed.  This worked fine up to a point, but after a while, cockatrices
stopped coming, and I found out that they had been genocided.  I understand
from what I've read lately that this is a feature, not a bug.  So anyway, I've
been experimenting with ways to reduce the number of cockatrices I need.  One
way that seems to work very nicely is just to keep a pet cockatrice.  But that
leads to two of the wierdnesses.

Twice already, Rocky (my cockatrice) has been walking along, and encountered 
an energy vortex.  In past patch levels, this was enough to make me immediately
remove my ring of conflict, because any time a cockatrice was swallowed up, it
would cause a crash.  But I've noticed that in patch level 10, this has been,
for the most part, fixed.  So now, I've felt more comfortable keeping my ring
on.  But on the two occasions I mentioned, Rocky was swallowed up by the energy
vortex.  This killed the vortex, but immediately, there was another vortex 
right where the dead one had been.  It then swallowed up Rocky, and caused a 
crash.  The crash was recoverable, though, and when I started the game up 
again, and I went to investigate the scene of the accident, there were two 
statues of energy vortices.  This only seems to happen with energy vortices,
and it doesn't seem to always happen.  This, I would have to classify as a bug.
I hope that the dev team can fix this bug as well as they fixed all the other
cockatrice swallowing bugs.  It is quite convenient to have a pet cockatrice,
except for the fact that the game keeps crashing.

The second deviant behavior also involved Rocky.  He kills a lot of things, and
most things can't touch him without dying, so his potential hit points go up 
quite fast.  His current hit points don't go up every time his possible hit
points do, unlike with characters.  I guess this is a feature, as the thing 
doesn't actually go up levels, it just gains hit points with experience.  So
unfortuntately, when something comes along that can hit a cockatrice safely, he
only has 40 or 50 hit points to use, rather than 1500 or so.  So I have taken 
to carrying along potions of healing or extra healing.  Whenever I throw one of
these at Rocky, it breaks into pieces and he looks to be in good health again.
When I apply my stethoscope to him, it says that he has 1500 or so hit points,
that is, he's at max again.  But then something bad happens.  When he next gets
hit, or gains some hit points, it takes him back down to 50 or so hit points
again.  Every hit he takes after that does only the expected damage.

I'm not sure, but this seems more like a feature than a bug.  Otherwise, a pet
cockatrice could be entirely too powerful, and it would only take one little
potion to give him back his full 1500 or so hit points.  Also, it seems that
any hit points he gets by regenerating them are real hit points, and don't 
disappear.  It does seem unnecessarily cruel though to give me the impression
that I have a devastating cockatrice when I only have a good one.  Oh well.

Another thing I discovered was that if you wield a cockatrice and turn
something to stone, and then kill another creature with a spell, that one
also turns to stone.  You can continue turning creatures to stone with your
magic missiles, or whatever, until you attack something physically which does
not turn to stone.  This feature/bug has allowed me to economize on my corpses
quite nicely.

The final oddity just happened to me, and it confuses me quite a bit.  I can no
longer lift gold.  Not one gold piece.  I can, by use of bags of holding with 
negative weight, lift hundreds of thousands of gems, but I can't lift a single
gold piece.  I noticed this happening just after my pet blue dragon, which had
been creating the gold for me, was unfortunately killed in a cockatrice/ring of
conflict accident.  I can't understand what could have happened.  This one to 
me seems like a bug. 

If anyone out there has any clues as to what happened here, I would appreciate
some kind of response.

Bruce Abe 


